  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member writing a reply with the modern composer, I want the composer to stay above the keyboard after I insert a smiley from the smiley picker, so that I can keep typing without lowering the keyboard to find it again.\n\n### Observed (operator, 2026-11-20, device, `dev-swift` build)\n- Modern composer (docked card), open the smiley picker, insert a smiley.\n- Back in the editor, the composer sits **behind the keyboard**; it reappears only when the keyboard is lowered.\n\n### Suspects (merged 2026-11-19, to confirm, not a conclusion)\n| Commit | PR | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| `ced6568d` | #1223 (#1136) | the docked card's height follows `ComposerKeyboardRoom`: no room until the keyboard has shown once, and **a hidden keyboard keeps the last room**. The picker hides the keyboard and shows it again: the card may keep a stale room or position when the keyboard comes back |\n| `76d8ca46` | #1269 (#1177) | the smiley detail and the GIF confirmation are now pushed inside their panel, not a third sheet: the panel's dismissal path changed |\n\nRelated, not the same: #909 (the floating composer's smiley picker closes on the first tap), #910 (insertion point).\n\n### Scope\n1. Reproduce in the simulator (modern composer on, Réglages › Expérimental), read the keyboard-room and card-placement path at `ced6568d` and `76d8ca46`, name the culprit.\n2. Fix so that the card is placed above the keyboard after any panel (smiley, GIF, image) closes and the keyboard returns; no change to the legacy composer.\n3. A test that fails without the fix (the pure `ComposerKeyboardRoom` model: keyboard hidden by a panel then shown again).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- After inserting a smiley (and a GIF, an image) the card is above the keyboard, on iPhone and iPad, portrait and landscape.\n- The #1136 behaviour (the card grows with the reply up to the room left) is unchanged.\n- Device check listed on #893.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_"