   "body": "Analysis from a cloud session (read of `dev-swift` @ `0e8bb39`, no device, no fix attempted). Needs a Mac session (`host: mac-helps`) to reproduce first.\n\n**Read**\n- The pure model is consistent: `ComposerKeyboardRoom` ignores a hidden keyboard (height 0) and keeps the last height, so after the picker closes the room is the same. A unit test cannot go red for this issue.\n- The docked card is a `safeAreaInset(.bottom)` of the reader (`ReaderComposerPresenter`); its bottom is placed by SwiftUI's keyboard safe area, not by our code. \"Behind the keyboard until lowered\" looks like the reader's keyboard avoidance not being re-applied after the smiley panel (a sheet over the composer) closes. Suspect, not a conclusion.\n- #1269's change only affects what is pushed inside the panel; the panel is still a sheet, so the dismissal path is the same.\n\n**A Mac session must reproduce and capture**\n1. Simulator, Réglages › Expérimental › modern composer on, a reply in the reader (compact width), keyboard up.\n2. Open the smiley picker, insert a smiley: does the bar sit behind the keyboard? Same with a GIF and an image, and with the picker dismissed without inserting.\n3. At that moment read: the bar's frame in window coordinates, the keyboard frame (`keyboardFrameEndUserInfoKey` of the last `keyboardWillChangeFrameNotification`, and whether one fired at all after the dismissal), the reader's and the bar's `safeAreaInsets.bottom` (view debugger), and `ComposerKeyboardRoom.lastHeight` / `layout.availableHeight`.\n4. Whether `focused` was already `.text` when the sheet's `onDismiss` ran (no change, so no re-focus), and whether lowering and raising the keyboard fixes it.\n\nFix to be decided once the culprit is named.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
